# Walkthrough - MCQ Practice Service Data Integration

I have integrated real data from the database into the MCQ practice service, enabling users to select subjects, chapters, and topics with accurate question counts.

## Changes Made

### API Layer
- **[exam.ts](file:///c:/Users/User/Documents/monorepo-new/packages/api/src/routers/home/exam.ts)**:
    - Updated `getSubjectsWithChapters` to include topics within each chapter.
    - Added MCQ counts for each topic.
    - Switched ordering to `position` for consistency with other services.

### Frontend Layer
- **[mcq-practice-service.tsx](file:///c:/Users/User/Documents/monorepo-new/apps/home/modules/services/ui/views/mcq-practice-service.tsx)**:
    - Removed `subjectsData` mock constant.
    - Now consumes real data from `trpc.home.demoExam.getSubjectsWithChapters`.
    - Updated selection logic (subjects, chapters, topics) to work with database-driven IDs.
    - Enhanced hero section badges to display real counts for subjects, chapters, and total questions.
    - Fixed TypeScript linting errors in map callbacks.

## Verification Results

### Dynamic Data Loading
The component now correctly displays subjects, chapters, and topics fetched from the database.

### Selection & Filtering
Selection of subjects, chapters, and topics correctly updates the "Total Questions Available" counter and validates the "Start Practice" button based on the requested question count.

### Code Quality
TypeScript errors regarding implicit `any` types in map callbacks have been resolved by adding explicit types.
